# Pass "incompat-original": the original mod this one declares itself incompatible with, alone beside it.
#
# BlockHen.Animal.DustBunnies, Workshop 2659958183 - Dust Bunnies by 2blockdude and HendraGradeWood, which declares
# 1.1, 1.2 and 1.3 and nothing further. About.xml names it in incompatibleWith because the two define the same
# defNames. RimWorld does not refuse two mods that do: it keeps one copy and the mod that loads last owns it. This
# pass stages both and plays 07-original-mod-incompatibility, which asserts that ownership, so a green run says the
# incompatibility is still true.
#
# The original is listed here so that it is staged before the mod under test; the scenario asserts the order
# ("loads after") before it asserts the owner, and fails naming the order if the staging put them the other way.
#
# Nothing has to be downloaded. The staging script reads the Windows Workshop first, and the original is subscribed
# there with its 1.1, 1.2 and 1.3 folders (checked on 2026-09-24 by listing the folder, not by staging). The other
# Dust Bunnies in the Workshop, Crow's Crows.DustBunny (3480725900), is a different mod with no def in common and is
# not part of this pass.
BlockHen.Animal.DustBunnies   2659958183
